    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk about a new chapter. it doesn't feel like a new beginning, it just feels like the end of the road. like i've spent everything i had to get here and now i'm just... hollow. it's exhausting to keep pretending that there's something else worth fighting for when the biggest thing i ever wanted turned out to be nothing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense to feel hollow when you realize the only thing that gave your life energy was just a ladder to a room of your own. The exhaustion you feel isn't a failure, but the exhaustion of a hollow dream that has been important to you for a long time.\n\nYou don't have to immediately jump to a \"new\" idea just because the old structure is gone; the capacity to feel emptiness is a necessary step in understanding what you truly want to build.",
